--- body ---
## Context

Original goal: automate the last step of the bibliography pipeline
(related-work-note → bib-merge → local refs.bib → Zotero), which was
manual (File → Import).

Closed on 2026-05-13 as "out of scope for IDH" because the originally-
specified mechanism (Zotero Web API via Pyzotero, with PAT-based auth)
belongs in a research-project repo, not the harness.

Reopened on 2026-05-13 because a leaner approach turns out to be
in-scope for IDH: rather than calling the Zotero Web API, the skill
prepares a RIS file from one or more source documents and hands it to
`xdg-open`. The user's MIME associations decide whether it lands in
Zotero or a text editor — both are acceptable. No PAT, no Web API
dependency, no plugin install, no library-ID config. Skill is generic
and reusable across projects.

## Implementation (PR #180)

Skill `zotero-import` at `skills/zotero-import/SKILL.md`, backed by
`scripts/zotero-import.py` with three subcommands:

- `probe <pdf>...` — extract pdfinfo + first/last-page text + DOI /
  ISBN / handle / arXiv identifiers + naïve Zotero duplicate hits
  against the local SQLite (read-only, `?immutable=1`).
- `match` — refined Zotero lookup using the agent-extracted title.
- `write --out <ris> --entries-json <json>` — emit a combined RIS
  with TI in original language, ST for English short title, type-
  aware page-count handling, and `L1 file://` attachment.

The SKILL.md drives the judgement work: title extraction, online
identifier resolution (CrossRef / OpenLibrary / arXiv), web search
fallback, duplicate adjudication, English short-title generation.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `skills/zotero-import/SKILL.md` committed, invocable via Skill tool.
- [x] Dedupe against existing Zotero library by DOI or fuzzy title;
      surface attachment-basename matches with high confidence.
- [x] PDF attachment works (via RIS `L1 file://`; Zotero's *Linked
      Attachments* preference decides copy vs link).
- [x] No hardcoded secrets (no auth needed — Web API path not used).
- [x] End-to-end tested on six Vietnam Technology Catalogue 2026
      drafts (~/Technology Catalogues 2026 for public hearing/).

## Out of scope (deferred)

- Zotero Web API path (Pyzotero, PAT, `create_items()`). Original
  ticket scope; no longer planned. Use Zotero's own UI if API-level
  control is needed.
- Bib → Zotero import. Different input shape; bib-merge already covers
  the local-staging side, and Zotero's File → Import handles .bib
  natively.
- Zotero RDF output (`dc:relation` for Related items, `z:Collection`).
  Investigated 2026-05-13; rejected: `xdg-open` on Linux routes
  `application/rdf+xml` to the browser, not Zotero, which breaks the
  skill's "let the environment decide" contract. Conditions for
  revisiting documented in PR #180 discussion.
